# CVEs trivy reports that we deliberately accept, with rationale.
# Re-evaluate this file when the underlying packages get rebuilt with newer
# Go / upstream fixes — these are not permanent ignores.

# /usr/bin/gh (GitHub CLI) is compiled with an older Go stdlib (currently
# v1.26.2) than what `--ignore-unfixed` would let through. The CVEs are all
# DoS in code paths Sam doesn't exercise:
#   - LookupCNAME via cgo resolver (Sam doesn't process untrusted DNS)
#   - HTTP/2 SETTINGS infinite loop (Sam uses gh as a client, not server)
#   - ParseAddress / consumePhrase on email input (Sam doesn't parse mail)
#   - Dial NUL-byte panic on Windows (Sam runs on Linux)
# Fix arrives when GitHub publishes a gh build linked against Go 1.26.3+ or
# 1.25.10+. Until then, the affected paths are unreachable in our use.
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
